findings.body:
The test renders `GenericComponent<int>` but asserts the WebAssembly marker's `TypeName` and `Assembly` against `GenericComponent<string>`. `WebAssemblyComponentSerializer` writes `typeof(T).FullName`, which for `<int>` contains `System.Int32`, so `Assert.Equal` on `TypeName` fails.

::diff{file="src/Components/Endpoints/test/EndpointHtmlRendererTest.cs" lines="825-838"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `Assembly` assertion passes by accident because both generic instantiations come from the same assembly. The `TypeName` assertion is the one that breaks.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Endpoints/test/EndpointHtmlRendererTest.cs" lines="837-838"}
Assert.Equal(typeof(GenericComponent<int>).Assembly.GetName().Name, preambleMarker.Assembly);
Assert.Equal(typeof(GenericComponent<int>).FullName, preambleMarker.TypeName);

